                "t": "reveal",
                "label": "See the reasoning",
                "v": "The market environment is a legitimate partial mitigating factor — the below-market revenue growth context diagnosed in the analysis does explain part of the distribution. But 'the market' doesn't explain why these three reps were at 55% attainment when other tenured reps in comparable territory types were at 70-80% — the differential within comparable situations is where individual performance does matter. The advice to the Sales Director: acknowledge the market context in the review, be clear that the lower environment affected everyone, and then focus the performance conversation specifically on the gap between these three reps' outcomes and those of their most similar peers. The market argument explains why the bar was harder; it doesn't explain why some people cleared a hard bar and others didn't."
