                "t": "reveal",
                "label": "Reveal the model policies",
                "v": "<strong>Scenario A — Revenue attribution:</strong> Plan document defines a 'primary rep' and 'overlay rep' structure where each deal has a named primary owner at the time of initial opportunity creation in CRM. The primary rep earns 100% credit; an overlay (technical or specialist) rep earns a defined split (e.g. 50% credit) that doesn't reduce the primary rep's credit — funded separately from the company's overlay budget. Disputes about primary ownership: the timestamp of CRM opportunity creation is the definitive record — no retroactive re-attribution is permitted.\n\n<strong>Scenario B — Deal timing:</strong> Plan document specifies that revenue is booked in the period when the signed contract is received AND the order is entered in the system as confirmed revenue — both conditions must be met. A deal signed December 30th that enters the system January 2nd counts in Q1. No exceptions without documented Finance approval of accelerated revenue recognition, which requires the contract AND a cleared payment or confirmed purchase order.\n\n<strong>Scenario C — Mid-year territory change:</strong> Plan document specifies that any territory change mid-year entitles the affected rep to a pro-rated quota adjustment for the remaining months in the new territory, calculated at the time of the change and confirmed in writing to the rep. Q3 attainment in the previous example is assessed against the pro-rated target, not the original annual target."
