                "t": "reveal",
                "label": "Reveal model approach for Step 1",
                "v": "The global framework must establish:\n1. Global job architecture: 5 levels (Associate, Analyst, Manager, Director, VP/Head) across 5 job families (Editorial, Commercial, Technology, Operations, Corporate). 25 grade combinations, each with a written level descriptor.\n2. Global spread policy: ±15% at Associate/Analyst, ±20% at Manager, ±25% at Director, ±30% at VP.\n3. Global governance: Global TR sets framework and audits; country HR implements within approved bands; exceptions above the range maximum require Global TR approval with documented rationale.\n4. Global review calendar: April (primary global review cycle), October (market rate check, inflation adjustment where needed). High-inflation markets (Nigeria) may have additional interim check-ins as needed.\n5. Positioning philosophy: P50 for most roles; P65 for technology roles where Driftwood competes directly with tech sector employers; P75 not used as default but available with Global TR approval for specifically scarce skills."
