                "v": "Currency: All pay ranges and decisions are set and communicated in local currency. GBP reference conversion (as Driftwood's reporting currency) is used for: internal equity comparison at the global grade level, annual total payroll cost reporting to Finance, and expat package design if applicable. Exchange rates for reporting are refreshed quarterly; pay decisions are not adjusted mid-year for exchange rate movements.\n\nInflation cadence by market:\n- UK, South Africa, UAE: annual review at primary April cycle\n- Kenya, Ghana: annual review + October market check\n- Nigeria: semi-annual reviews (April and October) with interim inflation adjustment mechanism triggered by 10%+ 6-month CPI\n\nThe different review frequencies are approved globally, documented in the framework, and communicated to the Nigeria team specifically so they understand they're operating on a different cadence rather than discovering this through comparison with other markets."
